    "result_text": "The full suite is green: **68 tests, 0 failures, 0 errors, BUILD SUCCESS**.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented `ownerSegment` as a derived read-only field on the owner response, following the project's existing pattern for computed attributes (like `locality`, `timezone`, `ageBand`):\n\n1. **`Owner.java`** \u2014 added a `@Transient getOwnerSegment()` that returns `<TIER>_<AREA>`:\n   - `TIER` = `PREMIUM` when `getMembershipLevel() >= 3`, else `STANDARD`.\n   - `AREA` = `METRO` when `getRegion()` is a known region (NSW/VIC/QLD), else `REGIONAL` (i.e. when the region is `UNKNOWN`).\n\n2. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added the `ownerSegment` schema property (string enum of the four values, `readOnly`) to the owner response model. The DTO is generated from this spec, and MapStruct auto-maps the matching-name getter, so no mapper change was needed.\n\nBoth new tests in `Cp55Tests` pass (`STANDARD_METRO` for a Sydney/NSW owner, `STANDARD_REGIONAL` for an unknown city), and all 68 tests remain green.",
